  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Response in Cabo Delgado, Mozambique (Phase III)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For over four years, the province of Cabo Delgado in Mozambique has experienced brutal attacks by armed groups, while neighbouring provinces of Nampula, Niassa, Zambezia and Sofala are seeing a spillover of displacement. Armed conflict and natural hazards are expected to put an additional strain on already vulnerable communities and to remain key drivers of humanitarian needs in the coming years. The effects are more severe on vulnerable groups such as persons with disabilities, the elderly, and children. This also affects women and girls, who have unique health concerns and protection needs in situations of displacement. In order to address the acute needs of displaced and vulnerable migrants in Cabo Delgado, IOM is providing a comprehensive and integrated health, water, sanitation and hygiene, camp coordination and camp management, displacement tracking, mental health and psychosocial support, and shelter intervention, with the main objective to ensure dignified, safe and secure living conditions and basic services for vulnerable populations affected disasters driven by natural hazards and conflict, and to contribute to empowered and resilient individuals and communities in northern Mozambique.</narrative>
  </description>
